  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">REINTRODUCTION AND SURVEILLANCE OF THE SCARLET MACAW IN LOS TUXTLAS, VERACRUZ, AND THE CONSERVATION OF NATIVE SPECIES WITH COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION V</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THIS PROJECT AIMS TO SUPPORT THE CONSERVATION EFFORTS IN LOS TUXTLAS, VERACRUZ, OF SCARLET MACAWS BY CONTINUING ACTIONS THAT ENSURE THE CONSERVATION OF THIS NEW NATURAL POPULATION. THESE ACTIONS WILL INCLUDE REINTRODUCING TWO NEW GROUPS RAISED IN CAPTIVITY (AT LEAST 50 NEW YOUNG MACAWS), MONITORING FREE MACAWS, AND SUPPORTING THE REPRODUCTION OF FREE-RANGE MACAWS BY SUPERVISING NEST BOXES ALREADY PROVEN IN THEIR EFFECTIVENESS. THE HATCHING OF 50 NEW MACAWS BORN IN THE WILD CAN BE PROJECTED BETWEEN NATURAL AND ARTIFICIAL NESTS IN TWO YEARS. THIS WILL INCREASE THE POPULATION FROM 320 TO 420 FREE MACAWS.IN ADDITION, THE ACTIVITIES WE PROPOSE TO MONITOR THE FREE POPULATION IN AT LEAST THREE RELEASE SITES. IN THE REPRODUCTIVE SEASON (SIX MONTHS), MONITOR NATURAL NESTS AND PLACE AT LEAST 20 NEST BOXES ANNUALLY IN AREAS PROTECTED BY THEIR OWNERS UNDER OUR SUPERVISION. RECORD THE REPRODUCTIVE SUCCESS OF THE NEST BOXES. WE HAVE LEARNED THAT THE ARTIFICIAL NEST BOXES NEED MAINTENANCE TO ENSURE THEIR SUCCESS, AND THIS IS LABOR INTENSIVE BECAUSE AS WE HAVE MORE AND SINCE THEY ARE IN DIFFERENT AREAS, MORE TIME IS REQUIRED. STILL, THE INVESTMENT IS SIGNIFICANT FOR THE MACAWS.THE AWARENESS CAMPAIGN HAS BEEN VERY EFFECTIVE BUT MUST BE EXPANDED TO SERVE MORE COMMUNITIES.</narrative>
  </description>
